 we also need to respond to current discussion about B vs D. We can either maintain D or shift.\n\nWe have our own notes: Candidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills. Also from earlier we have \"Candidate D is regarded as arrogant\" and \"relatively weak leadership skills\". Also \"Candidate D is considered moody\" and \"loner\". Those are from Agent 3's answer. So we have many concerns.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills, can be uncooperative, grumpy, can be pretentious, weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks. No decision quality evidence.\n\nCandidate A: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education, 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew, excellent attention (implied), concern for others above everything.\n\nCandidate C: can anticipate dangerous situations, able to see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized.\n\nWe need to bring in maybe Candidate A's reliability and quick decision making, and crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty. Compare to D and B.\n\nWe need to decide vote. Let's evaluate: For long-distance pilot, reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nCandidate A: reliability 100% (strong), creates positive atmosphere (crew cooperation), quick correct decisions (decision quality), excellent attention (attention), but difficulty communicating ideas (communication), egocentric (attitude), not willing to further education (adaptability). No stress resilience evidence, no technical competence evidence. So missing key.\n\nCandidate C: anticipates dangerous situations (decision quality), sees complex connections (technical), excellent spatial vision (technical), very good leadership (crew cooperation), but not good at taking criticism (cooperation), unorganized (reliability?), no stress resilience evidence, no reliability evidence.\n\nCandidate D: problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but arrogance, weak leadership, moody, loner, no stress resilience, no decision quality evidence.\n\nCandidate B: conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good weather assessment (technical), computer skills (technical), but uncooperative, grumpy (crew cooperation, communication). No decision quality evidence.\n\nThus B seems strongest overall despite interpersonal issues. A has strong reliability and decision speed but lacks stress resilience and technical competence. C has strong technical and leadership but lacks reliability and stress resilience. D has problem solving but interpersonal issues and lack of stress resilience.\n\nThus likely B remains best. As Agent 1, we originally shifted to D, but now after seeing A and C, maybe we reconsider. We can argue that A's reliability and quick decision making are valuable, but lack of stress resilience is a gap. We could ask for stress resilience evidence for A. But we may not have it. So we may keep D or shift to B.\n\nGiven the panel currently leaning B (2 votes), we might align with majority, but we need to provide reasoning. We can say we still see D's strong problem solving and responsibility, but his interpersonal issues are more severe than B's, and we lack evidence of stress resilience for D. Therefore I revert to Candidate B.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: Agent 2 and 3 argued for B, citing stress handling and reliability. I can say I agree with their points, and note that D's lack of stress resilience and crew cooperation concerns outweigh his strengths.\n\nThus vote B.\n\nProvide explicit facts: D's arrogance, weak leadership, moody, loner; B's very conscientious, handles stress well, good weather assessment, excellent computer skills.\n\nExplain why B is better.\n\nThus produce public message and metadata JSON with vote Candidate B."}
